# CODEOWNERS — who is responsible for which part of Haris.
#
# This is the written answer to the mentor's "who is responsible when something fails?".
# GitHub uses it to auto-request a review from the listed owner on any pull request that
# touches a matching path, and a red build in an area points at a named owner rather than
# "someone should look at it".
#
# The split mirrors the two working lanes: P1 owns the security core and the evaluation,
# P2 owns notifications, CI and deployment. Listing both people on every path would answer
# the question no better than having no file at all.
#
# Syntax:  <path-pattern>   <@owner> [@more-owners]
# Order matters: the LAST matching rule wins, so the catch-all goes first.

# Default owners for anything not matched by a more specific rule below.
*                        @zdk02 @bhb06

# P1 lane — the security core and the evaluation.
/haris/agents/           @zdk02
/haris/orchestrator/     @zdk02
/haris/policy/           @zdk02
/demo_app/eval/          @zdk02
/EVAL_DESIGN.md          @zdk02

# P2 lane — notifications, CI, deployment.
/haris/notify/           @bhb06
/NOTIFICATIONS.md        @bhb06
/.github/                @bhb06
/haris-infra.yaml        @bhb06
/Dockerfile              @bhb06
/verify-deployment.ps1   @bhb06
/teardown.ps1            @bhb06
/report/deployment-notes.md  @bhb06